---
import '../styles/global.css';

interface Props {
	title?: string;
}

const { title = 'GitCardX' } = Astro.props;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
		<title>{title}</title>
		<link
			href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;600;700;800&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
			rel="stylesheet"
		/>
		<link rel="icon" href="/images/logo-github-card-generator.webp" />
		<link
			rel="stylesheet"
			href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.2/css/all.min.css"
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<!--
THESIS: Building a card is a pipeline, not a form — filling fields in reads
like watching a GitHub Actions run turn from pending to passing.
OWN-WORLD: near-black graphite (#0b0d10), teal (#2dd4bf) as the one active/
build accent, semantic status pills (gray pending, amber running, green
passing, red failing) driving real field validity, JetBrains Mono for stage
labels/status text, Manrope for prose and headings.
STORY: a visitor recognizes the shape of a CI run instantly; each panel is a
pipeline "stage," the live card preview is the run's build artifact.
FIRST VIEWPORT: a stage-rail (horizontal desktop, vertical mobile) linking
Configure → Style → Assets nodes into the card-preview artifact node, each
node's pill reflecting that panel's real validity.
FORM: seed key ccac258b, candidate 3 of 7 (CI Pipeline / Status Graph),
user's own top pick over the assigned PCB/circuit direction and the
standard safe default.
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the
finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
-->
		<slot />
	</body>
</html>
